SELFHOST-CLEANROOM-1 — the Flutter revision the supported state actually depends on
Measured ON the qualification machine (2026-09-04), because the revisions
involved are not fetchable anywhere else — which is the point.

  record flutter_selector             e64eb0af52e1c43c3b21a39556d789538d0df9b3
    its bin/internal/engine.version   cd848320d605ff8af5060cabf9a8d1b35853f752   <- SUPERSEDED cell

  runtime checkout actual HEAD        5b180d224df04a267a19888c3f344474e243b382
    its bin/internal/engine.version   f85251f344600ae08196925a174e9cff8f0ff18e   <- SUPPORTED cell

  refs pointing at that HEAD          0
  present in the local mirror         NO — it exists only in the runtime checkout

  where e64eb0af itself lives:
    runtime Flutter remote            file:///Users/mendell/shorebird/selfhost/cdn/mirrors/flutter.git
    ref in that mirror                refs/heads/selfhost/3.44.8-v13
    author                            Shorebird selfhost <selfhost@example.invalid>
    subject                           candidate(6d): pin engine.version to the v13 cell cd848320

CONSEQUENCE. The verifier check "Flutter engine.version (committed blob)
selects the recorded cell" reads HEADs blob, so it is satisfied by WHATEVER
HEAD carries the right bytes — it does not pin a revision. The supported
state therefore depends on an unrecorded, unpushed commit, and an operator
who cloned the RECORDED selector would select the superseded cell.
